{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:6569895283c096fc8960544b3ad5e51a", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 12, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Updated `backup.sh` to complete the missing copy step.\n\nWhat it does now:\n- Reads the backup destination from the `DEST` environment variable.\n- Fails early with a clear message if `DEST` is unset.\n- Creates the dated tarball with `tar -czf logs-$STAMP.tar.gz logs/`.\n- Copies the tarball with `scp` for `host:path` destinations and `cp` for local/mount destinations.\n- Confirms both the tarball and destination after a successful copy.\n\nI also validated the script with `sh -n` and a local end-to-end test (logs → tarball → copied into a destination directory).\n\nSet `DEST` in the cron environment before tonight’s run, e.g.:\n\n```sh\nDEST=/mnt/backups /path/to/backup.sh\n# or\nDEST=user@backup-host:/backups /path/to/backup.sh\n```\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:8fdb42128bcbec69b40d5b691157f684"}
